HST Office: open MathType 4-7 equations as Math formulas when the user asks for it.

New option Office.Common/Filter/Microsoft/Import/MathType5ToMath (default off). When it is on,
.doc/.xls/.ppt (msfilter) and .docx/.rtf (writerfilter) convert "Equation.DSMT4" OLE objects.
A formula that fails to convert keeps its OLE object. In Writer the converted formula is a
normal Math object on the Math baseline; Word's run position shift only applies to the OLE
objects that stay. The DOCX/RTF logic lives in sw/source/writerfilter/hst/.

A converted equation keeps the scale Word shows it at: the shown size over the size of its
preview picture, which MathType makes at 100 % (.docx shape, .rtf \objh/\pichgoal); in .doc the
PICF vertical scale (my), as LibreOffice wrote the picture size of its own .doc files in twips
where Word reads 1/100 mm. MathType's point sizes in the formula are multiplied by it unless it
is within 5 % of 100 % (sw/source/core/hst/formulashownsize.cxx, shared by writerfilter and the
ww8 reader). The shown size is not compared with the formula's: MathType's box is taller than
Math's at the same size.

An equation kept as an OLE object keeps its data when the document is saved as .rtf (OLE 1.0
\objdata with the compound file byte for byte, the picture in \result), so MathType can still
edit it; LibreOffice's RTF export wrote only the picture (sw/source/core/hst/mathtypeoledata.cxx).
That picture has the shown size at 100 %: the RTF import sizes an object by its picture's goal.
The RTF import keeps the OLE data of equations (ProgID "Equation.*") in table cells too: the
object is buffered with the cell (RTFBufferTypes::HstOleObject) and sent when the cell is
replayed. LibreOffice read only the picture of objects in tables (fdo#53594), so saving again
lost the equation; other OLE objects in tables are unchanged.
